I know that the new reviewer is a WIP. But, I am still creating this issue because this is a niche use-case and I feel that there is a fairly high chance that the issue won't be solved otherwise.

My notetype uses the following script to hide the type answer box if the card doesn't have any HTML element with the class "type_ans". This works on Anki Desktop and on AnkiDroid's old reviewer (with `Advanced → Type Answer Into Card` enabled). However, this doesn't work on AnkiDroid's new reviewer.

```html
<script>
var typeElement = document.querySelector("#type");
var backElement = document.querySelector("#back");
var backContent = backElement.innerHTML;
var regex = /\btype_ans\b/;

if (!regex.test(backContent)) {
   typeElement.style.display = "none";
} 
</script>
```

